# DRAFT CITATION.cff for the new Delegation Assurance + Evidentiary Assurance repository.
# Not yet placed at its final path. Replace REPO2_NAME and REPO2_URL once the repository
# name is decided (see open-questions.md, item 1).
#
# Why `type: software` and `references:` here, not `type: dataset` or a bare `type: article`
# at the root:
#
# The CFF 1.2.0 schema restricts the ROOT-level `type` key to exactly two values,
# `software` or `dataset` (verified against the schema guide,
# github.com/citation-file-format/citation-file-format/blob/1.2.0/schema-guide.md).
# There is no root-level `article` type. The current AP repo's CITATION.cff sets
# `type: dataset` at the root, which fit AP (a benchmark/data artifact with an
# accompanying manuscript). This repository is different: it holds two manuscripts and
# their supporting executable artifacts (schemas, fixtures, validators), with no primary
# dataset. `type: software` (the schema default) better describes the repository itself --
# the executable artifact is what a citation to the *repository* actually points at.
#
# Neither paper should be named as the repository's single `preferred-citation`: CFF
# allows only one `preferred-citation` block, and privileging either Delegation Assurance
# or Evidentiary Assurance over the other would misrepresent a repository built to hold
# them as a pair. Instead, both are listed under `references:` (a list, unlimited size),
# which is the correct field for "other works this citation file should point readers to"
# without picking a favourite. Each entry uses `type: unpublished` because, at draft time,
# neither paper has been submitted (Delegation Assurance's venue decision is approved but
# submission has not happened; Evidentiary Assurance has been through two review rounds
# under an unnamed AI-governance-journal target with no venue-decision record yet -- see
# open-questions.md item 4). Update each entry's `type` to `article` and add `doi`,
# `journal`, `volume`, and `issue` fields once accepted; do not leave `unpublished` sitting
# in a citation file for a paper that has since been published.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository's schemas, fixtures, validators, or manuscript drafts, please cite the relevant paper below."
title: "Delegation Assurance and Evidentiary Assurance"
authors:
  - family-names: Reynolds
    given-names: Brett
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0073-7195"
type: software
date-released: "REPLACE-WITH-SPLIT-DATE"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BrettRey/REPO2_NAME"
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: "Delegation Assurance for AI Systems: Typed Authorization Semantics and Comparative Evaluation"
    authors:
      - family-names: Reynolds
        given-names: Brett
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0073-7195"
    year: 2026
    notes: "Targeting Minds and Machines (Springer); not yet submitted as of the 2026-07-24 venue decision record."
  - type: unpublished
    title: "Evidentiary Assurance for Delegated Authority in AI Systems"
    authors:
      - family-names: Reynolds
        given-names: Brett
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0073-7195"
    year: 2026
    notes: "Through two external-review rounds (major to minor revision) targeting an AI-governance journal as of 2026-07-24; no venue-decision record filed yet."
